From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:06:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] test(catalogue): read the catalogue's guard as a
 conjunction, not an adjacency
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red: he-asked-for-six-and-got-an-empty-shelf (culprit 0e2ff096)
  the seed reaches the shelf, not just a variable
  › NEGATIVE — and the catalogue stands down with the other authors
    pinned `if (!copyProvidersRationing && seedFields.length`

Decision: P. 0e2ff096 inserted two more stand-down terms between the two
names: `!modelUnavailableDuringBuild` (from 154e231d, the same term the
copy and section authors carry) and `!unifiedTables` (a 3+ entity system
renders TablesAdmin; RecordsApp is dormant, so there is no shelf to seed).
Both make the catalogue stand down MORE; the rationing term is untouched.

The test now finds the `if` that directly guards the authorCatalogue
require (nothing but `try {` between them), requires it to be a pure
conjunction (no `||`), and requires `!copyProvidersRationing` and
`seedFields.length` among its terms — so rationing alone stands it down,
whatever terms are added.

Non-vacuity:
  catalogue-no-rationing: `!copyProvidersRationing` removed from the guard
    ✕ NEGATIVE — and the catalogue stands down with the other authors
    Expected value: "!copyProvidersRationing"
    Received array: ["!modelUnavailableDuringBuild", "!unifiedTables", "seedFields.length", "!input?.skipAuthoredCopy"]
    RESTORED: sha256 identical
  catalogue-rationing-optional: `(!copyProvidersRationing || seedFields.length > 6) && ...`
    ✕ NEGATIVE — and the catalogue stands down with the other authors
    Expected substring: not "||"
    RESTORED: sha256 identical

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
---
 ...asked-for-six-and-got-an-empty-shelf.test.ts | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/api/src/__tests__/he-asked-for-six-and-got-an-empty-shelf.test.ts b/api/src/__tests__/he-asked-for-six-and-got-an-empty-shelf.test.ts
index 5f912b73..965c377a 100644
--- a/api/src/__tests__/he-asked-for-six-and-got-an-empty-shelf.test.ts
+++ b/api/src/__tests__/he-asked-for-six-and-got-an-empty-shelf.test.ts
@@ -259,7 +259,22 @@ describe('the seed reaches the shelf, not just a variable', () => {
     it('NEGATIVE — and the catalogue stands down with the other authors', () => {
         //  It spends the same rationed fuel as the section and copy authors;
         //  guarding two of three is the «one layer, two generators» class.
-        expect(TOOL).toMatch(/if \(!copyProvidersRationing && seedFields\.length/);
+        //
+        //  Read as the condition that guards the catalogue author, not as an
+        //  adjacency: 0e2ff096 added more reasons to stand down between the
+        //  two names this used to pin. The guard is a pure conjunction, and
+        //  rationing is one of its terms — so rationing alone stands it down.
+        const call = TOOL.indexOf('const { authorCatalogue');
+        expect(call).toBeGreaterThan(0);
+        const ifAt = TOOL.lastIndexOf('if (', call);
+        const open = TOOL.indexOf(') {', ifAt);
+        //  …and it is THE guard: nothing but `try {` between it and the call.
+        expect(TOOL.slice(open + 3, call).replace(/\s+/g, '')).toBe('try{');
+        const guard = TOOL.slice(ifAt + 'if ('.length, open).replace(/\s+/g, ' ');
+        expect(guard).not.toContain('||');
+        const terms = guard.split('&&').map((t: string) => t.trim());
+        expect(terms).toContain('!copyProvidersRationing');
+        expect(terms).toContain('seedFields.length');
     });
 });
 
